      "artist": "Gabor Eszes (UED77)",
      "description": "Panoramic view from the National Park Service's New River Gorge Bridge Overlook, opposite from Fayetteville, WV, USA. On the left, the New River is visible as it flows through its deep gorge towards the viewer and continuing to the right. The sight of the river is blocked by trees in the middle. On the right, the New River Gorge Brige can be seen as it towers above the valley.\n\nThe panorama consists of ten components: five forming a top row, and five on the bottom. It was assembled with Hugin 0.5 using Autopano-SIFT and nona as the stiching engine. The resulting TIFF was edited to correct two blending errors. The final file was saved to Progressive JPEG with a 95% quality setting in Irfanview.",
